@page "/demo/env-config/orders/net10"
@layout DemoLayout

<h1>Recent orders</h1>

@* What the same list read on .NET 10, recorded from its repro. The server passed the
   variable with a hand-written Blazor.start script, the only way it had. *@
<Net10Recording Sdk="10.0.102" Request="GET /, the server passing Orders__ApiUrl"
                Repro="wasm-env-vars-config" Note="Read from the page by Playwright once WebAssembly started.">
    <p><span class="badge">Running on WebAssembly</span>
        Calling <code>https://staging-api.northwind.test/orders?take=5</code></p>
    <p class="error">Couldn't reach https://staging-api.northwind.test/orders
        <small>(TypeError: Failed to fetch)</small></p>

    <table class="sources" data-sources>
        <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>appsettings.json</th><th>Variable</th><th>Config[key]</th></tr></thead>
        <tr><th>Orders:ApiUrl</th><td>https://staging-api.northwind.test/orders</td>
            <td>demo/env-config/api/orders</td>
            <td class="miss"><b>https://staging-api.northwind.test/orders</b></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Orders:PageSize</th><td>5</td><td>none</td><td><b>5</b></td></tr>
    </table>

    @* .NET 10's own fix: one line in the client, plus a package. *@
    <p class="note">Configuration providers: <code>JsonStreamConfigurationProvider</code> only.
        With <code>AddEnvironmentVariables()</code> and its package added, and the same script,
        <code>Config["Orders:ApiUrl"]</code> was <b>demo/env-config/api/orders</b>.</p>
</Net10Recording>
